      "content": "I'm having some trouble with the specificity required for dermatological coding in our new billing cycle. We're seeing a lot of cases involving atypical presentations of cutaneous lesions—specifically those with irregular borders, heterogeneous pigmentation, and unusual textural changes that don't clearly fall under standard melanocytic nevus categories. Can you walk me through the hierarchy for selecting the most specific ICD-10 code when the morphology is ambiguous or presents with atypical features?",
